{"title":"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a2573fcb2b0b0566a35fd80ebda15de2dc3f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathcal{F}_n)_{n \\geq 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> be a sequence of functions going from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f210b79b44ba0f06662d484e9c142ae4f05bed6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f210b79b44ba0f06662d484e9c142ae4f05bed6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> defined recursively by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151ed5601aa309fad4e7f2bdc0fee19a4f50e188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{F}_1(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd057c104d32e88e03e12d779f8d64f4db06d32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathcal{F}_k(n)=\\sum_{d|n}\\mathcal{F}_{k-1}(d)\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"41\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df9cf1d6f6e2474e61796d7425ac78ce112893b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Compute the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83af98ea83c7bbb60a7cdbb76fdf4218811833c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\mathcal{F}_{2019}(864)}{\\mathcal{F}_{2019}(648)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the function on the right is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19db4f964753d03642db7f8fc9d1a3a1a55b4686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{k}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />’s sum function, so if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19db4f964753d03642db7f8fc9d1a3a1a55b4686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{k}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is multiplicative so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947667d714398b6b193ffabd77a81e06969e4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{k+1}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />. Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b427fddf577079298003ee9723096db775e3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{1}(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> is multiplicative, it is not hard to see using induction that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19db4f964753d03642db7f8fc9d1a3a1a55b4686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{k}(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are multiplicative too.\n</p><p>Therefore we can just consider one prime and its exponent. Say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec754149234c24b67addd073791456e6b52fb7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p_1^{e_1}\\cdots p_k^{e_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab47ef219c4b1bb96997c73835dfb031c05ef07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{1}(p^e)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501b95c55dde4b2e795c0f39ef8b6d665dae302b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_2(p^e)=1+1+1+\\cdots +1=e+1=\\binom{e+1}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"372\" height=\"53\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5609af9d5ba6995fa88aaeffd67bc7206698505d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_3(p^e)=\\sum_{i=0}^e \\binom{i+1}{1} =\\binom{e+2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"256\" height=\"53\" /> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hockey_stick_identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hockey stick identity\">Hockey Stick Identity</a>. We can continue this process (summing and using the hockey stick identity for each exponent) to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0a9e10969105cd0e9c68e2c3249ff5d7ea6f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{2019}(p^e)=\\binom{e+2018}{2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"185\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/933f821dd1cde8748cafe1ac5bf0bc983a9b7cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$864=2^5 3^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f4c3802956099096dcef31f9e74f8f2d511342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$648=2^3 3^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19b07f1fccd2a586b20c5cee635965c751aa652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\binom{2023}{2018}\\binom{2021}{2018}}{\\binom{2021}{2018}\\binom{2022}{2018}}=\\dfrac{2023 \\cdot 2022 \\cdot 2021 \\cdot 2020 \\cdot 2019 \\cdot 24}{2022 \\cdot 2021 \\cdot 2020 \\cdot 2019 \\cdot 120} = 2023 \\cdot \\frac{24}{120} = \\frac{2023}{5} = 404.6 \\rightarrow \\boxed{404}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"686\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I (page does not exist)\">2019 CIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:MAC_Notice&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:MAC Notice (page does not exist)\">Template:MAC Notice</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011146\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 165/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1445/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 115/2